> Identifying HTTP methods
	
-> HTTP Methods
		GET - Retrieves data from a resource.
		PATCH - Applies partial changes to a resource.
		OPTIONS - Retrieves information on the types of request methods that can be used on a resource.
		POST /api/tasks - Creates a new task.
		PUT - Replace the Entire Resource.
		DELETE /api/tasks/1 - Deletes a task.
		HEAD - Retrieve headers only (same as GET without body)
	- the built-in HTTP verbs list in Burp Intruder. 

-> Identifying supported content types	
	To change the content type, modify the Content-Type header
		- use the Content type converter BApp to automatically convert data submitted within requests between XML and JSON. 

